# XML lexical scopes, paired by compiled symbol dispatch. A recipe for an XML
# file says "format xml" and then only what its source's parts are.
#   an element holds nodes, and is named by its tag's name
#   an attribute is a name and its text, the text with XML's references resolved and its quotes off
#   character data, a reference and a CDATA section are text, side by side one text
#   the prolog (declaration, document type), comments, processing instructions and end tags are how the file is
#   written down, and not of its tree
grammar lp_xml_scopes
scope STag end ETag name Name empty EmptyElemTag
scope-space CharData
scope-misc XMLDecl doctypedecl Comment PI StyleSheetPI XmlModelPI
resolve xml
quotes AttValue
trim
node STag group name Name context .
node EmptyElemTag group name Name context .
node Attribute value name Name text AttValue
node CharData text join
node EntityRef text join
node CharRef text join
node CData text raw join
node XMLDecl skip
node doctypedecl skip
node Comment skip
node PI skip
node StyleSheetPI skip
node XmlModelPI skip
node ETag skip
node CDStart skip
